# Naming Conventions

## File Naming
- **React Components**: Use PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`, `ModalDeleteConfirmation.tsx`)
- **Custom Hooks**: Use `use` prefix with camelCase (e.g., `useGetAllRole.tsx`, `useMutateAddRole.tsx`)
- **Page Components**: Use `page-` prefix with kebab-case (e.g., `page-role.tsx`, `page-user.tsx`)
- **Type Definitions**: Use camelCase (e.g., `type.ts`, `fetching.ts`)

## Folder Naming
- **Feature Folders**: Use kebab-case (e.g., `master-data/`, `stock-opname/`, `activity-log/`)
- **Component Folders**: Use kebab-case (e.g., `modal-delete-confirmation/`, `button/`)
- **Utility Folders**: Use lowercase (e.g., `hooks/`, `libs/`, `utils/`, `types/`)

## Variable Naming
- **Variables & Functions**: Use camelCase (e.g., `userData`, `handleSubmit`, `isLoading`)
- **Constants**: Use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`)
- **Boolean Variables**: Use `is`, `has`, `can`, `should` prefixes (e.g., `isVisible`, `hasPermission`)

## Type Naming
- **Interfaces**: Use PascalCase (e.g., `UserData`, `StockOpnameForm`)
- **Type Aliases**: Use PascalCase (e.g., `UserRole`, `ApiResponse<T>`)
- **Enums**: Use PascalCase with UPPER_CASE values (e.g., `UserStatus.ACTIVE`)

## Import/Export
- **Named Exports**: Use PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions
- **Default Exports**: Use PascalCase for components, camelCase for hooks
- **Import Statements**: Use exact casing as exported names

## React Query Hooks
- **Query Hooks**: Use `useGet[Entity]` pattern (e.g., `useGetAllRole`, `useGetAllUser`)
- **Mutation Hooks**: Use `useMutate[Action][Entity]` pattern (e.g., `useMutateAddRole`, `useMutateDeleteRole`)
